<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abbas ibn Firnas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 810–887</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abbas ibn Firnas was an Andalusi polymath of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> descent at the court of the Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> in the ninth century. A poet, astronomer and inventor, he is credited with a method of cutting rock crystal and with a planetarium-like device, and according to a later account by al-Maqqari he attempted to fly with a feathered apparatus, injuring himself on landing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abbas-ibn-firnas.jpg" alt="Abbas ibn Firnas" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eulogia Merle · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Armen_Firman_Abb%C3%A1s_Ibn_Firn%C3%A1s_(MUNCYT,_Eulogia_Merle).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
